# Findings the CI image scan (trivy, ci.yml "build images") ignores, each with the reason and the
# condition for removing it. Unfixable Debian findings are already excluded by `ignore-unfixed`.
#
# cryptography 46.0.7 -> fixed in 50.0.0. Blocked: gridstatus 0.36.0 (the ISO queue parsers) pins
# cryptography<47, so the patched release does not resolve. Same exception as pip-audit's
# PYSEC-2026-3552/3553/3554 in ci.yml; tracked in docs/00-PLAN.md (2026-09-15, "First CI runs").
# Remove the day gridstatus relaxes the pin.
CVE-2026-69247
# cryptography 46.0.7: the same gridstatus pin blocks 49.0.0 and 48.0.1 (second scan, 2026-09-15).
CVE-2026-69249
GHSA-537c-gmf6-5ccf
# lxml 5.4.0: gridstatus 0.36.0 pins lxml~=5.3, so the 6.x fix does not resolve. lxml parses source
# HTML the connectors fetch, so this is the exception that matters most; see docs/00-PLAN.md
# follow-up (vendor the two gridstatus parsers if the pin is not relaxed within a month).
CVE-2026-41066
# wheel 0.45.1 and jaraco.context 5.3.0 are the copies vendored inside setuptools 78.1.1
